AudD  ·  profile default
                 │ Help › Keys
 1 Recognize     │  Getting started  Guide  Commands >Keys< Exit codes  Links 
 2 Now playing   │ Moving around
 3 Streams       │   Menu on the left, page on the right. Arrows move, Enter
 4 Recognitions  │   goes in, Esc comes back.
 5 Account       │   The menu is the sidebar; Help, Streams, Recognitions, and
 6 Settings      │   Account have a tab bar above their page. On a choice ‹ like
*7 Help          >   this ›, ←/→ change it and ← on its first option goes back.
                 │   When a text field is selected, you are typing in it:
                 │   letters, digits, and symbols go in, ←/→ move the cursor (←
                 │   at its start goes back), ctrl+u clears it, and esc stops
                 │   typing. Recognize opens typing in Input; other pages open
                 │   with no text field selected, so 1-7 jump to a section. A
                 │   saved value, such as the callback URL, is changed only
                 │   after enter or e, and esc puts the old value back. Enter in
                 │   a form's last text field runs it (in Add a stream, enter in
                 │   ID adds it; the box below is optional). What a page can do
                 │   is on its buttons: tab (or ↓ from the end of the page)
 [ Commands ]    │   reaches them, ←/→ move between them, enter presses one. A
 [ Keys ] q quit │ ↓ 115 more lines below

←/→ tabs  ↓ open  esc back  ? keys
ctrl+k runs any audd command